      ⍝ Signing off. )OFF prints the APL\360 sign-off: the time and date the
      ⍝ session ended, then how long it was connected and how much processor
      ⍝ time it used. All three come from the clock, so the reg-rs filter
      ⍝ masks their values and keeps their shape; see docs/testing.md.
      ⍝ APL\360 also named the port and the user and carried totals to date.
      ⍝ sw-apl has no accounts and keeps no such records, so it does not.
      'THE SESSION DID SOME WORK'
